    <AdditionalInfo>TRANSFER FUNCTIONS HAVE BEEN ROTATED INTO GEOGRAPHIC COORDINATES.
Data were collected by the University of
Washington and the Geological Survey of Canada with
funding from the U.S. National Science Foundation and
the Geological Survey of Canada. All data were
collected in geomagnetic N/E. Tipper data were rotated
to geographic north while impedance data were
separately rotated to the geoelectric strike direction
for each profile. Impedance data were subsequently rotated
by Paul Bedrosian to geographic north and combined with
tipper data to produce final EDI files with all data
in geographic north. Suggested citation: Wu, N.,
Booker, J.R., Unsworth, M.J., Jones, A.G. (1992).
&quot;Magnetotelluric Transfer Functions over the
North American Central Plains, North Dakota (NOD)
profiles, United States&quot;</AdditionalInfo>
